<title>MEXICO: Gasoline imports up to 75,000 BPD in 1997 - Pemex.</title>
<headline>Gasoline imports up to 75,000 BPD in 1997 - Pemex.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico should import up to 75,000 barrels per day of gasoline through the end of the year, the head of Mexico's oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex), Adrian Lajous said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;In general terms we can be sure the levels (of gasoline imports) will be about 70,000 to 75,000 barrels a day,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
<p>He added that growing domestic demand for gasoline and greater unleaded gasoline consumption showed the need to boost Mexico's refinery system.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 7902))</p>
